.TH tuc4 n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuc4
.PP
Parses a Mermaid C4 diagram (\fBC4Context\fR, \fBC4Container\fR, \fBC4Component\fR, \fBC4Dynamic\fR, \fBC4Deployment\fR) into a \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR model, so a C4 diagram can render natively (SVG or PNG) through the pure\-Tcl engine — no browser. It is one of the graph\-type parsers the \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR facade dispatches to; you normally call \fBtuflow::toPng\fR / \fBtuflow::toSvg\fR rather than this module directly.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tuc4 0.1
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tuc4::parse text      ;# -> tudiagram model dict
.CE
.PP
The result is a \fBtudiagram\fR model and is rendered with \fBtclutils::tudiagram::toSvg\fR / \fBtoPng\fR (or via the \fBtuflow\fR facade).
.SS "Supported syntax (Mermaid subset)"
.CS
Person(id,"name",...)  Person_Ext(...)        -> rounded box (actor)
System(...) SystemDb(...) SystemQueue(...)     -> box
Container(...) Component(...) and *Db/*Queue   -> box
*_Ext variants                                 -> box
Rel(from,to,"label",...)                       -> edge from -> to, labelled
BiRel / Rel_U|Rel_D|Rel_L|Rel_R(from,to,"...") -> edge (direction hint ignored)
title <text>                                   -> diagram title
*_Boundary(id,"label") { ... }                 -> flattened (inner kept)
UpdateElementStyle / UpdateRelStyle / Update…  -> ignored
.CE
.PP
An element's display label is its \fB"name"\fR (the first quoted argument); the leading id token becomes the node id.
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tuc4
package require tclutils::tudiagram

set src {C4Context
    title Internet Banking
    Person(customer, "Customer", "A bank customer")
    System(banking, "Banking System", "Web app")
    System_Ext(email, "E-mail System")
    Rel(customer, banking, "Uses")
    Rel(banking, email, "Sends", "SMTP")
}
set m [::tclutils::tuc4::parse $src]
::tclutils::tudiagram::writePng $m c4.png -scale 3
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
v1 limitations (honest): boundaries (\fBEnterprise_Boundary\fR, \fBSystem_Boundary\fR, \fBContainer_Boundary\fR, \fBBoundary\fR, \fBDeployment_Node\fR, \fBNode\fR) are flattened — their inner elements are kept, the boundary box itself is not drawn; the technology/description arguments are not shown (only the name); \fBBiRel\fR renders as a single\-headed edge; the directional \fBRel_U/D/L/R\fR hints are ignored (\fBtudiagram\fR lays the graph out top\-down).
.IP \(bu
Companion: \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR (renderer), \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR (dispatch).
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUC4 <REASON>}\fR — \fBEMPTY\fR (no elements found).
